    {
      "id": "claim_b28c296da2d746708dfad2b0d519db6a",
      "statement": "The application applies Flyway migrations at startup by default — spring.flyway.enabled=true with locations=classpath:db/migration, baseline-on-migrate=true, baseline-version=0, and UTF-8 encoding in the shipped application.properties, which the Docker and lite install paths rely on — so pre-Flyway databases such as a docker/ecshopx.sql import are baselined at version 0 instead of replaying history, with execution history recorded in flyway_schema_history; no shipped profile turns startup migration off, so a local developer wanting manual control runs bin/make-migration migrate or overrides the flag through the usual Spring mechanisms (--spring.flyway.enabled=false on the command line or the SPRING_FLYWAY_ENABLED environment variable).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://bin/make-migration#L42-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1858ecdb63802eda0abb2b92e7dd903ff37995dc1bf52859d7c7811c73ee4924:"
