    {
      "id": "claim_8daeb3007a974be285eb8b57f518eebd",
      "statement": "Secondary and unique indexes are generated only from explicit metadata — @MpTable(indexes/uniqueIndexes) entries with @MpIndex(name, columns, unique, lengths) and @MpField(unique = true) (which yields a uniq_<table>_<column> key) — never invented for stock-annotated entities; when two domain classes map the same table, the generator keeps the richer mapping (more columns, then more indexes, then more primary keys, then the shorter source path) and warns about the ignored one; every generated CREATE TABLE ends with ENGINE = InnoDB DEFAULT CHARACTER SET utf8mb4 COLLATE utf8mb4_unicode_ci.",
